  "Question": "A bag contains only blue balls and green balls. There are \\(6\\) blue balls. If the probability of drawing a blue ball at random from this bag is \\(\\dfrac14,\\) then the number of green balls in the bag is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(12 \\)",
    "B": "\\(18 \\)",
    "C": "\\(24 \\)",
    "D": "\\(30 \\)",
    "E": "\\(36 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Each ball is equally likely to be drawn, so the probability of blue equals the fraction of all balls that are blue. A probability of \\(\\frac14\\) means the six blue balls make up one of four equal shares of the total number of balls.\n\nEach share therefore contains six balls, so the total number is\n\\[\n4\\cdot6=24.\n\\]\nThe bag contains only blue and green balls. Removing the six blue balls from the total leaves\n\\[\n24-6=18\n\\]\ngreen balls, choice B.",
